    "duration": "Annual benefit. Winners of the annual scholarship hold the canteen and accommodation benefits from 01.10.2026 to 30.09.2027; winners of the semestre filtro scholarship from 01.10.2026 to 31.03.2027; doctoral and specialisation-course winners from 01.01.2027 to 31.12.2027. The scholarship is open to students enrolled for the achievement of their FIRST degree, so it is recompeted each academic year rather than granted for a fixed multi-year term.",
    "deadline": "13.00 (Italian time) on 7 September 2026 for the a.a. 2026/2027 call, covering laurea triennale, laurea magistrale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico; the window opened at 12.00 on 20 July 2026. For students enrolled on doctoral and specialisation courses the window ran from 25 September 2026 to 13.00 on 16 November 2026.",
    "deadline_date": "2026-09-07",
    "deadline_precision": "day_and_time",
    "application_period": "Annual competitive call for academic year 2026/2027: applications open at 12.00 on 20 July 2026 and close at 13.00 on 7 September 2026 for first-cycle (laurea triennale) and second-cycle (laurea magistrale, laurea magistrale a ciclo unico) students. A later window runs from 25 September 2026 to 13.00 on 16 November 2026 for students enrolled on doctoral and specialisation courses. The previous a.a. 2025-26 call closed on 6 September 2025.",
    "application_method": "Separate application, not automatic on admission. Candidates complete the domanda di borsa di studio through the DSU Toscana Sportello Studente portal at https://sportellostudente.dsu.toscana.it. The University of Pisa does not award this scholarship and does not process it: its own page tells students to request the borsa di studio from the DSU and links to dsu.toscana.it.",
    "status": "closed",
    "is_verified": true,
    "last_verified_date": "2026-10-03",
    "description": "Il Diritto allo Studio Universitario in Toscana is administered by the Azienda Regionale Diritto allo Studio Universitario (ARDSU, 'DSU Toscana'), a regional agency, whose scholarship (borsa di studio) is the principal need-based funding instrument for students at the University of Pisa. The University of Pisa does not award it: its scholarships page states that students can request a borsa di studio from the DSU and links to the DSU call. The scholarship gives winners a monetary quota that varies with the family's economic condition and with whether the student is in sede, pendolare or fuori sede, plus free access to DSU canteen services, free accommodation for winners subject to availability (EUR 262.50 per month for eligible non-winners) and exemption from the regional right-to-study tax. The a.a. 2026/2027 call is promoted within Giovanisì, the Regione Toscana project for youth autonomy, and co-financed by the regional Toscana FSE+ 2021-2027 programme. The application closes at 13.00 on 7 September 2026 for laurea triennale, laurea magistrale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico students, so the cycle for the verification date is closed.",
    "best_fit": "Students who are, or intend to be, enrolled on their first degree at the University of Pisa and whose families meet the ISEE and ISPE economic thresholds of the call, particularly fuori sede students who need an accommodation place and free canteen meals, and students in a first laurea triennale or laurea magistrale a ciclo unico year. Not suitable for anyone already holding an equivalent-level title, not suitable for students who have enrolled on a master's degree after already graduating at that level, and not a tuition-fee scholarship: no amount is published for the cash quota on the pages read, and tuition is only affected indirectly through any separate ISEE-based exemption.",
    "funding_amount": null,
    "funding_currency": null,
    "funding_period": null,
    "eligibility_summary": "The concorso is open to students regularly enrolled for the achievement of their FIRST degree on laurea, laurea specialistica/magistrale, dottorato di ricerca and scuole di specializzazione courses at the universities of Florence, Pisa and Siena and at the other higher institutes, art academies and conservatories of the Tuscany region. The University of Pisa states the same rule from its own side: all students who wish to enrol or are already enrolled on a laurea course at the University of Pisa and who apply, provided they do not already hold an academic title of the same level. Economic requirements are expressed through the ISEE and ISPE indicators of the DSU, and the call also sets merit requirements (art. 5.3 of the call, verified by the Agency through official acquisition of valid credits for the enrolled course). Students with a recognised disability under art. 3 of Law 104/1992 or with invalidity of 66% or more, students with minor children and nationally competitive athletes have dedicated merit requirements and higher income limits; first-year students with a disability are exempt from the merit-based decadenza that applies to other students.",
    "eligibility": [
      "Regularly enrolled, or intending to enrol, for the achievement of the FIRST degree on a laurea course at the University of Pisa",
      "Not already in possession of an academic title of the same level (the University of Pisa states that a student enrolling on a laurea magistrale cannot receive the scholarship if they already hold a laurea magistrale)",
      "Economic requirements based on the ISEE and ISPE indicators of the DSU, as specified in the call",
      "Merit requirements specified in the call (art. 5.3), verified by the Agency through official acquisition of valid credits registered for the enrolled course in 2026/2027",
      "A DSU valid for facilitated right-to-study services, subscribed by 7 September 2026, relating to the student requesting the benefit",
      "Accommodation and canteen benefits are reserved for fuori sede students (status determined by provenance and public-transport travel time to the course location) and are subject to availability of places",
      "Enhanced conditions for students with a disability under art. 3 of Law 104/1992 or with invalidity of 66% or more: extended benefit duration, dedicated merit requirements, scholarship integration, priority for accommodation and accessible residences, and the option of a rent contribution instead of a place and of monetising the canteen service",
      "Enhanced income limits and merit requirements for students with minor children, and specific merit requirements for nationally competitive athletes",
      "Open to international students: the call is issued in Italian, English, French, Arabic and Chinese, and the DSU keeps a dedicated 'Studenti Stranieri' page",
      "Not eligible: students who already hold an equivalent-level title, which forfeits the benefit for a further degree at the same level"
    ],
    "coverage": [
      "Cash monetary quota, varying with the family's economic condition and with in sede / pendolare / fuori sede status (amount not published on the pages read)",
