    "english_requirement": null,
    "selection_notes": "Selection is by economic condition and merit, not by nationality or academic competition alone. The Agency assigns the benefit after a need analysis built on the ISEE and ISPE indicators of the DSU, and applies merit requirements set by the call; the Agency states it verifies achievement of the merit requirement through official acquisition (acquisizione d'ufficio) of the valid credits registered for the course the student is enrolled on in 2026/2027. The outcome produces a ranking of vincitori (winners) and idonei non vincitori (eligible non-winners): both categories get free canteen access and exemption from the regional fee; the accommodation place is free for winners and charged at EUR 262.50 per month to eligible non-winners, and the cash quota is paid to winners. Results for laurea triennale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico first years were published as provisional on 30 September 2026 and definitive on 4 November 2026 for the scholarship alone, with a further definitive date of 30 November 2026.",
    "image_url": "https://www.unipi.it/wp-content/uploads/Raggruppa-3020.svg",
    "image_source_url": "https://www.unipi.it/campus-e-servizi/servizi/borse-di-studio-e-posti-alloggio-dsu-toscana/",
    "image_source_type": "official_logo",
    "image_alt_text": "Università di Pisa",
    "image_verified_at": "2026-10-03",
    "notes": "PROVENANCE, stated plainly because the assigned award name is misleading. The b03 assignment names 'Borse di Studio - Universita di Pisa' on host unipi.it, but the University of Pisa does not award this scholarship and does not run it. The University's own page 'Borse di studio e Posti Alloggio DSU Toscana' (https://www.unipi.it/campus-e-servizi/servizi/borse-di-studio-e-posti-alloggio-dsu-toscana/) opens with 'Gli studenti possono richiedere una borsa di studio del DSU, Azienda Regionale Diritto allo Studio Universitario' and links to https://www.dsu.toscana.it/borsa-di-studio, and the University's other scholarships page states that 'Il Diritto allo Studio Universitario in Toscana è gestito dal DSU Toscana'. The awarding body is therefore ARDSU (Azienda Regionale Diritto allo Studio Universitario, P.IVA 05913670484, registered office Viale Antonio Gramsci 36, 50132 Firenze), a regional agency acting under articles 3 and 34 of the Italian Constitution, and the call is promoted within Giovanisì and co-financed by Toscana FSE+ 2021-2027. Recording it as a University of Pisa scholarship would be a provenance error of exactly the kind recorded for b46 (Zois state scholarships vs the University of Ljubljana), so this record names ARDSU as the awarding body and keeps the University of Pisa pages as the eligible-institution source. NO MONETARY AMOUNT IS RECORDED and funding_amount is null on purpose: the DSU page states the quota 'varia in relazione alla condizione economica e alla condizione di studente in sede, pendolare e fuori sede' and publishes no euro figure for it; the only figures published on the pages read are the EUR 262.50 monthly accommodation tariff for eligible non-winners and the instalment percentages (20%/30%/50%) and dates. The deadline is 13.00 on 7 September 2026 for first- and second-cycle students, so as at the verification date of 2026-10-03 the cycle is CLOSED and the next cycle is expected in the first half of July 2027 for academic year 2027/2028 (the previous call closed 6 September 2025, and the window has consistently opened in late July). The DSU page does not print a timezone; the 13.00 deadline is read as Italian local time (Europe/Rome) because the page is the Italian awarding agency's own call and the companion documents give Italian dates throughout. The University of Pisa page describes the scholarship as including 'esonero dalle tasse universitarie' while the DSU page narrows this to 'esonero dalla tassa regionale per il diritto allo studio universitario'; because the awarding body's own wording is the narrower one and the call PDF was not opened, this record does NOT claim a general tuition waiver and records tuition_coverage as false, with the discrepancy flagged in institution_check_required. The call is issued in Italian, English, French, Arabic and Chinese, but the English-language call (EN_bando borsa alloggio 2026-2027.pdf) was not opened, so no English-language evidence and no ISEE/ISPE threshold figures are recorded. The English-language Unipi page https://www.unipi.it/en/campus-e-servizi/services/scholarship/ was not fetched, and no English-language test requirement is claimed. The dedicated DSU page for foreign students, https://www.dsu.toscana.it/studenti-stranieri, was not fetched, so non-EU eligibility detail, the tassa regionale amount, the merit-requirement credit thresholds and the bando's art. 5.3 and art. 9 conditions are all recorded as unconfirmed rather than estimated. The logo is the University of Pisa institutional mark served from the unipi.it domain itself, not a DSU asset, and it is used here as the image for the entry because the assigned slot's host is unipi.it and the University is the eligible institution whose page this record is keyed to."
  },
