    "application_cycle": "a.a. 2026/2027 concorso per borsa di studio e posto alloggio. The page is headed 'Borsa di studio a.a. 2026-2027'. The application window for laurea triennale, laurea magistrale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico students ran from 12.00 on 20 July 2026 to 13.00 on 7 September 2026; for doctoral and specialisation students from 25 September 2026 to 13.00 on 16 November 2026.",
    "deadline_central": "2026-09-07T13:00",
    "deadline_central_display": "fino alle ore 13.00 del 7 settembre 2026 (for laurea triennale, laurea magistrale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico); the later doctoral/specialisation window closed at 13.00 on 16 November 2026",
    "deadline_central_timezone": "Europe/Rome",
    "deadline_institutional": null,
    "deadline_note": "The DSU Toscana call page states the application window as opening at 12.00 on 20 July 2026 and closing at 13.00 on 7 September 2026 for students enrolled, or intending to enrol, on laurea triennale, laurea magistrale and laurea magistrale a ciclo unico courses. A separate window opens on 25 September 2026 and closes at 13.00 on 16 November 2026 for students enrolled on doctoral and specialisation courses. The deadline for holding the DSU is the same 7 September 2026 date. No timezone is printed; Italy observes CEST on 7 September 2026, so the deadline is read as Europe/Rome local time. As at the verification date of 2026-10-03 the 13.00 7 September 2026 deadline is in the past, which is why the status is CLOSED and the next cycle is expected in the first half of July 2027 (the equivalent a.a. 2025-26 call closed on 6 September 2025).",
    "status": "CLOSED",
    "status_note": "The a.a. 2026/2027 concorso closed at 13.00 Italian time on 7 September 2026 for first-cycle and second-cycle degree students, which is in the past as at the verification date of 2026-10-03. The Agency is still running the 2026/2027 contest through its instalment and results schedule, so the award itself remains live for admitted winners rather than closed: canteen and accommodation benefits run to 30 September 2027, the first instalments were due on 10 November and 31 December 2026, and the definitive rankings for scholarship holders were due on 4 and 30 November 2026. The next full cycle is expected to open in the second half of July 2027 for academic year 2027/2028; the previous call (a.a. 2025-26) closed on 6 September 2025, and the Agency publishes each year's call on the same page.",
    "funding_amount": null,
    "funding_currency": null,
    "funding_period": null,
    "funding_duration": "The scholarship is recomputed each academic year for students enrolled on their first degree. For the 2026/2027 contest, free canteen access and accommodation run from 01.10.2026 to 30.09.2027 for winners of the annual scholarship, from 01.10.2026 to 31.03.2027 for winners of the semestre filtro scholarship, and from 01.01.2027 to 31.12.2027 for doctoral and specialisation-course winners.",
    "tuition_coverage": false,
    "tuition_coverage_note": "No tuition waiver is confirmed. The DSU Toscana page scopes the fee reduction narrowly: winners and eligible non-winners 'spetta, inoltre, l'esonero dalla tassa regionale per il diritto allo studio universitario' — that is, exemption from the regional right-to-study fee, not from the University of Pisa tuition or registration fees. The University of Pisa page phrases the same benefit more broadly as 'esonero dalle tasse universitarie'. Because the awarding agency's own wording is the narrower one and the call PDF (Bando di concorso a.a. 2026/2027) was not opened for this record, this record does not claim that university tuition is waived, and the wider University of Pisa phrasing is flagged as unconfirmed in institution_check_required. Any tuition reduction a student obtains is a separate consequence of the ISEE-based exemption rules published by the University, not of this scholarship.",
