    "citizenship_residency": "No nationality restriction. Eligibility is set by economic condition (ISEE and ISPE), by enrolment for a first degree at a Tuscan institution, and by the merit requirements of the call. The call is published in Italian, English, French, Arabic and Chinese, which is the Agency's own signal that it is addressed to students outside the Italian-speaking population, and the Agency maintains a dedicated 'Studenti Stranieri' page whose content was not read for this record. The residence distinction that matters for benefits is not nationality but commuting status — in sede, pendolare or fuori sede — determined by provenance and public-transport travel time to the course location.",
    "international_eligibility": "Open to students of any nationality, including students without Italian citizenship, subject to the same ISEE/ISPE and merit requirements. The call itself is issued in five languages including English, Arabic and Chinese. Non-EU nationals face one practical constraint that is economic rather than legal: the DSU used to determine the ISEE and ISPE indicators is the Italian DSU, so a student from abroad must be able to obtain one valid for facilitated right-to-study services by 7 September 2026, which is something to confirm with the Agency's dedicated foreign-student page (https://www.dsu.toscana.it/studenti-stranieri) before relying on this scholarship. No separate international quota is published on the page.",
    "degree_levels": [
      "Bachelor's",
      "Master's",
      "PhD and specialisation courses"
    ],
    "study_mode": "Not specified on the pages read. The DSU page states the concorso is open to students 'regolarmente iscritti per il conseguimento del primo titolo di studio' on laurea, laurea specialistica/magistrale, dottorato di ricerca and scuole di specializzazione courses, and does not distinguish full-time from part-time enrolment, so no study-mode condition is recorded.",
    "research_requirement": null,
    "subject_or_agency_requirement": "No subject restriction. The concorso is open across the courses of the universities of Florence, Pisa and Siena and the other Tuscan higher institutes, art academies and conservatories, so all fields at the University of Pisa are covered. Two specific provisions are subject-linked in effect rather than by field: the 'Semestre filtro' scholarship applies to Medicine, Veterinary Medicine and Dentistry students, and the Agency notes that regional filtering rules affect students enrolled on those courses in other regions. Course fees and other charges vary by course and are not covered by the scholarship.",
    "application_method": "Separate, competitive application. The candidate completes the domanda di borsa di studio through the DSU Toscana Sportello Studente portal at https://sportellostudente.dsu.toscana.it, and must hold a DSU valid for facilitated right-to-study services subscribed by 7 September 2026. There is no automatic consideration on admission to the University of Pisa.",
    "application_route": "Submit the online domanda di borsa di study and domanda di posto alloggio through the DSU Toscana Sportello Studente portal (https://sportellostudente.dsu.toscana.it, 'Domanda / Application 2026/2027'), having first subscribed to a DSU. The call documents, including the English 'Call for application', are downloadable from the 'Bando di concorso 2026/2027' section of the DSU page. The University of Pisa's role is only to identify and link to this route from its own scholarships pages.",
