      "Italian or SEPA-area IBAN of a current account or prepaid card held in the student's own name, declared in the application"
    ],
    "english_requirement": null,
    "english_requirement_note": "No English-language test requirement is published for this scholarship on any page read, so the field is null rather than estimated. What the official pages do show is that the call documents themselves are multilingual: the 'Bando di concorso 2026/2027' section of the DSU page offers the bando in Italian, an English 'Call for application', French, Arabic and Chinese, alongside FAQ, DSU regulations and the online application in the same languages. The English call PDF was not opened, so no language or qualification requirement specific to non-Italian speakers is claimed. Admission to the University of Pisa has its own separate requirements, which were not read for this record.",
    "selection_criteria": [
      "Economic condition, expressed through the ISEE and ISPE indicators of the DSU",
      "Merit requirements set by the call (art. 5.3), verified by the Agency through official acquisition of the valid credits registered for the enrolled course in 2026/2027",
      "Commuting status — in sede, pendolare or fuori sede — determined by provenance and public-transport travel time to the course location, which sets the amount of the quota",
      "Enrolment for the first degree and absence of an equivalent-level title",
      "For students with a disability under art. 3 of Law 104/1992 or with invalidity of 66% or more: dedicated merit requirements commensurate with their condition, higher income limits and scholarship integration, with first-year students with a disability exempt from the merit-based decadenza",
      "For students with minor children: higher income limits and specific merit requirements; for nationally competitive athletes: specific merit requirements"
    ],
    "selection_weighting": null,
    "duration": "One academic year at a time, recomputed annually, because the benefit is reserved for students enrolled for the achievement of their FIRST degree. For the 2026/2027 contest the free-canteen and accommodation benefits run from 01.10.2026 to 30.09.2027 for annual winners, from 01.10.2026 to 31.03.2027 for semestre filtro winners, and from 01.01.2027 to 31.12.2027 for doctoral and specialisation winners.",
    "award_holder_conditions": [
      "The beneficiary must be enrolled for the achievement of the FIRST degree, so holding an equivalent-level title forfeits the benefit",
      "The monetary quota is paid in instalments, and the second instalment is conditional on reaching the merit requirement of art. 5.3 of the call",
      "Payments are made by bank transfer to a current account or prepaid card with an Italian or SEPA-area IBAN in the beneficiary student's own name; if the student does not yet hold an IBAN it must be communicated through the online form by the mandatory deadline of 31 December 2028",
      "In the event of decadenza or reduction of a benefit the Agency notifies the outcome by ticket through the Sportello Studente, giving a mandatory 10-day window for rebuttals or clarifications, followed by formal notice by raccomandata setting out the measure, any amount to be repaid, the sanction and the payment method",
      "Repayment of sums and payment of any sanction may be made in a single solution or in instalments of up to 24 monthly instalments with a minimum of EUR 60 per instalment, under art. 13 of the Regolamento accertamenti; missing two consecutive instalments forfeits the instalment arrangement and the whole residual balance becomes payable immediately",
      "No service bond, work obligation or return-to-Tuscany obligation is published; the obligations published are academic merit and repayment on forfeiture, not service"
    ],
    "supplements_or_initiatives": [
      "DSU Toscana 'Posto alloggio': the companion accommodation service governed by the same call, free for scholarship winners and EUR 262.50 per month for eligible non-winners, subject to availability.",
      "DSU Toscana 'Contributo affitto': a separate rent contribution listed among the Agency's services that can, in the cases provided for by the call, be elected by students with a disability as an alternative to a residence place.",
      "DSU Toscana 'Mobilità internazionale': a separate international mobility contribution listed among the Agency's services, outside this record.",
      "DSU Toscana 'Monetizzazione dei servizi' and 'Mantenimento dei servizi': further mechanisms for converting or retaining services, listed by the Agency and not read for this record.",
      "University of Pisa 'Collaborazioni part-time (150 ore)': part-time collaborations for students in services for the student community (library, laboratory, administration, archive), governed by the Regolamento for part-time student collaborations at https://www.unipi.it/wp-content/uploads/partime.pdf. This is a work opportunity, not a scholarship, and is described on the University's scholarships-and-support page alongside the DSU route.",
      "University of Pisa 'Premi e borse di studio': a separate University page listing prizes and scholarships, not read for this record.",
      "Invest Your Talent in Italy: a programme listed under the University's international relations programmes and reachable from its international-registration section, whose content was not read for this record."
    ],
